  "summary": "Australian senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore of the Nick Xenophon Team will resign after discovering she holds British citizenship by descent from her mother, who gained UK citizenship in 1983 under the British Nationality Act. Kakoschke-Moore, born in Darwin in 1985, had previously been advised she was not eligible for British citizenship and described the revelation as heartbreaking and surprising. She will ask that the High Court determine how her Senate vacancy is filled and intends to continue running for the NXT with hopes of returning to the Senate. A recount would likely see NXT candidate Tim Storrer elected, but party leader Nick Xenophon says legal advice suggests the case may fall into untested territory due to a recent High Court ruling involving Hollie Hughes. Xenophon and colleagues expressed devastation at her departure but believe her political career will continue."
}
```

